Q: React useEffect dependency array causes infinite re-render when syncing state with props A: <p>If the value you want to display in the counter comes from outside of it, just make it a controlled component (i.e. without internal state):</p>
<pre class="lang-ts prettyprint-override"><code>type CounterProps = {
  value: number;
  onClick: () =&gt; void;
};

function Counter({ value, onClick }: CounterProps) {
  return &lt;button onClick={onClick}&gt;{value}&lt;/button&gt;;
}
</code></pre>
<p>And use it like:</p>
<pre class="lang-ts prettyprint-override"><code>function App() {
  const [value, setValue] = useState(0);

  return (
    &lt;&gt;
      &lt;Counter value={value} onClick={() =&gt; setValue(prev =&gt; prev + 1)}/&gt;
    &lt;/&gt;
  );
}
</code></pre>
<p><a href="https://react.dev/learn/sharing-state-between-components" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Read: lifting the state up</a></p>

Q: How to get a scrollable table with a fixed header in shadcn/ui? A: <p>I do this for sticky header ! trust me:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;ScrollArea className=&quot;w-full h-96&quot;&gt;
&lt;Table&gt;...&lt;/Table&gt;
      &lt;/ScrollArea&gt;
</code></pre>
<pre><code>
function Table({ className, ...props }: React.ComponentProps&lt;&quot;table&quot;&gt;) {
  return (
    &lt;table
      data-slot=&quot;table&quot;
      className={cn(&quot;w-full caption-bottom text-sm&quot;, className)}
      {...props}
    /&gt;
  )
}
</code></pre>
<pre><code>function TableHeader({ className, ...props }: React.ComponentProps&lt;&quot;thead&quot;&gt;) {
  return (
    &lt;thead
      data-slot=&quot;table-header&quot;
      // className={cn(&quot;[&amp;_tr]:border-b&quot;, className)}
      className={cn(&quot;sticky -top-px z-1 bg-secondary [&amp;_tr]:border-b&quot;, className)}
      {...props}
    /&gt;
  )
}
</code></pre>
